---Transcoding job resource.
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.Job
---@field fillContentGaps? boolean Optional. Insert silence and duplicate frames when timestamp gaps are detected in a given stream.
---@field templateId? string Input only. Specify the `template_id` to use for populating `Job.config`. The default is `preset/web-hd`, which is the only supported preset. User defined JobTemplate: `{job_template_id}`
---@field startTime? string Output only. The time the transcoding started.
---@field name? string The resource name of the job. Format: `projects/{project_number}/locations/{location}/jobs/{job}`
---@field state? gcp.transcoder_v1.JobStateEnum Output only. The current state of the job.
---@field outputUri? string Input only. Specify the `output_uri` to populate an empty `Job.config.output.uri` or `JobTemplate.config.output.uri` when using template. URI for the output file(s). For example, `gs://my-bucket/outputs/`. See [Supported input and output formats](https://cloud.google.com/transcoder/docs/concepts/supported-input-and-output-formats).
---@field inputUri? string Input only. Specify the `input_uri` to populate empty `uri` fields in each element of `Job.config.inputs` or `JobTemplate.config.inputs` when using template. URI of the media. Input files must be at least 5 seconds in duration and stored in Cloud Storage (for example, `gs://bucket/inputs/file.mp4`). See [Supported input and output formats](https://cloud.google.com/transcoder/docs/concepts/supported-input-and-output-formats).
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the job was created.
---@field mode? gcp.transcoder_v1.JobModeEnum The processing mode of the job. The default is `PROCESSING_MODE_INTERACTIVE`.
---@field batchModePriority? number The processing priority of a batch job. This field can only be set for batch mode jobs. The default value is 0. This value cannot be negative. Higher values correspond to higher priorities for the job.
---@field error? gcp.transcoder_v1.Status Output only. An error object that describes the reason for the failure. This property is always present when ProcessingState is `FAILED`.
---@field optimization? gcp.transcoder_v1.JobOptimizationEnum Optional. The optimization strategy of the job. The default is `AUTODETECT`.
---@field endTime? string Output only. The time the transcoding finished.
---@field ttlAfterCompletionDays? number Job time to live value in days, which will be effective after job completion. Job should be deleted automatically after the given TTL. Enter a value between 1 and 90. The default is 30.
---@field config? gcp.transcoder_v1.JobConfig The configuration for this job.
---@field labels? gcp.transcoder_v1.StringMap The labels associated with this job. You can use these to organize and group your jobs.

