---Segment settings for `ts`, `fmp4` and `vtt`.
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.SegmentSettings
---@field segmentDuration? string Duration of the segments in seconds. The default is `6.0s`. Note that `segmentDuration` must be greater than or equal to [`gopDuration`](#videostream), and `segmentDuration` must be divisible by [`gopDuration`](#videostream).
---@field individualSegments? boolean Required. Create an individual segment file. The default is `false`.

---Sprite sheet configuration.
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.SpriteSheet
---@field format? string Format type. The default is `jpeg`. Supported formats: - `jpeg`
---@field endTimeOffset? string End time in seconds, relative to the output file timeline. When `end_time_offset` is not specified, the sprites are generated until the end of the output file.
---@field rowCount? number The maximum number of rows per sprite sheet. When the sprite sheet is full, a new sprite sheet is created. The default is 0, which indicates no maximum limit.
---@field startTimeOffset? string Start time in seconds, relative to the output file timeline. Determines the first sprite to pick. The default is `0s`.
---@field filePrefix? string Required. File name prefix for the generated sprite sheets. Each sprite sheet has an incremental 10-digit zero-padded suffix starting from 0 before the extension, such as `sprite_sheet0000000123.jpeg`.
---@field quality? number The quality of the generated sprite sheet. Enter a value between 1 and 100, where 1 is the lowest quality and 100 is the highest quality. The default is 100. A high quality value corresponds to a low image data compression ratio.
---@field columnCount? number The maximum number of sprites per row in a sprite sheet. The default is 0, which indicates no maximum limit.
---@field interval? string Starting from `0s`, create sprites at regular intervals. Specify the interval value in seconds.
---@field totalCount? number Total number of sprites. Create the specified number of sprites distributed evenly across the timeline of the output media. The default is 100.
---@field spriteWidthPixels? number Required. The width of sprite in pixels. Must be an even integer. To preserve the source aspect ratio, set the SpriteSheet.sprite_width_pixels field or the SpriteSheet.sprite_height_pixels field, but not both (the API will automatically calculate the missing field). For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata, provide the width, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates the height per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
---@field spriteHeightPixels? number Required. The height of sprite in pixels. Must be an even integer. To preserve the source aspect ratio, set the SpriteSheet.sprite_height_pixels field or the SpriteSheet.sprite_width_pixels field, but not both (the API will automatically calculate the missing field). For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata, provide the height, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates the width per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata and swaps the requested height and width for the output.

---@alias gcp.transcoder_v1.SpriteSheetList gcp.transcoder_v1.SpriteSheet[]

---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.Status
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field details? gcp.transcoder_v1.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

