---Video stream resource.
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.VideoStream
---@field h265? gcp.transcoder_v1.H265CodecSettings H265 codec settings.
---@field vp9? gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9CodecSettings VP9 codec settings.
---@field h264? gcp.transcoder_v1.H264CodecSettings H264 codec settings.

---VP9 codec settings.
---@class gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9CodecSettings
---@field hlg? gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9ColorFormatHLG Optional. HLG color format setting for VP9.
---@field frameRate? number Required. The target video frame rate in frames per second (FPS). Must be less than or equal to 120.
---@field pixelFormat? string Pixel format to use. The default is `yuv420p`. Supported pixel formats: - `yuv420p` pixel format - `yuv422p` pixel format - `yuv444p` pixel format - `yuv420p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format - `yuv422p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format - `yuv444p10` 10-bit HDR pixel format - `yuv420p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format - `yuv422p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format - `yuv444p12` 12-bit HDR pixel format
---@field gopFrameCount? number Select the GOP size based on the specified frame count. Must be greater than zero.
---@field heightPixels? number The height of the video in pixels. Must be an even integer. When not specified, the height is adjusted to match the specified width and input aspect ratio. If both are omitted, the input height is used. For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata, provide the height, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates the width per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
---@field widthPixels? number The width of the video in pixels. Must be an even integer. When not specified, the width is adjusted to match the specified height and input aspect ratio. If both are omitted, the input width is used. For portrait videos that contain horizontal ASR and rotation metadata, provide the width, in pixels, per the horizontal ASR. The API calculates the height per the horizontal ASR. The API detects any rotation metadata and swaps the requested height and width for the output.
---@field profile? string Enforces the specified codec profile. The following profiles are supported: * `profile0` (default) * `profile1` * `profile2` * `profile3` The available options are [WebM-compatible](https://www.webmproject.org/vp9/profiles/). Note that certain values for this field may cause the transcoder to override other fields you set in the `Vp9CodecSettings` message.
---@field rateControlMode? string Specify the mode. The default is `vbr`. Supported rate control modes: - `vbr` - variable bitrate
---@field frameRateConversionStrategy? gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9CodecSettingsFrameRateConversionStrategyEnum|string Optional. Frame rate conversion strategy for desired frame rate. The default is `DOWNSAMPLE`.
---@field gopDuration? string Select the GOP size based on the specified duration. The default is `3s`. Note that `gopDuration` must be less than or equal to [`segmentDuration`](#SegmentSettings), and [`segmentDuration`](#SegmentSettings) must be divisible by `gopDuration`.
---@field bitrateBps? number Required. The video bitrate in bits per second. The minimum value is 1,000. The maximum value is 480,000,000.
---@field crfLevel? number Target CRF level. Must be between 10 and 36, where 10 is the highest quality and 36 is the most efficient compression. The default is 21. **Note:** This field is not supported.
---@field sdr? gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9ColorFormatSDR Optional. SDR color format setting for VP9.

---@alias gcp.transcoder_v1.Vp9CodecSettingsFrameRateConversionStrategyEnum "FRAME_RATE_CONVERSION_STRATEGY_UNSPECIFIED"|"DOWNSAMPLE"|"DROP_DUPLICATE"

